# Logic vs UI

The only frontend app is **Next.js**. Keep logic out of the UI anyway.

Server state uses **TanStack Query** (`useQuery`, `useMutation`). Do not add Redux, Zustand, or ad-hoc fetch in components.

| Layer | Path | May import |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Logic | `frontend/logic/` | TypeScript, `fetch`, query keys. No JSX, Tailwind, or `next`. |
| Hooks | `frontend/hooks/` | `logic/` + `useQuery` / `useMutation`. No JSX or CSS. |
| UI | `frontend/components/`, `frontend/app/` | hooks, components, Next.js, Tailwind. No raw `fetch`. |

```ts
// ❌ BAD — fetch and rendering in the same file
export function Zones() {
  const [zones, setZones] = useState([]);
  useEffect(() => {
    fetch("/api/analysis/1/zones").then((r) => r.json()).then(setZones);
  }, []);
  return <ul>{zones.map((zone) => <li key={zone.id}>{zone.name}</li>)}</ul>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — fetcher in logic, hook in hooks, JSX in UI
const { data } = useAnalysisZones(analysisId);
```

- Do not add `.env` files or read `process.env` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Call the API with relative paths such as `/api/analysis`.
- Do not invent analysis data. Empty, loading, and error states are the only valid stand-ins.
